{"id": "en_house_fire_p1", "total": 61.35, "segments": [{"text": "If a fire alarm wakes you at night, do not stand up and run blindly through smoke.", "start": 0.0, "end": 3.46}, {"text": "Leo wakes up at 2 AM inside his home to a screeching smoke detector alarm above.", "start": 4.0, "end": 7.2}, {"text": "Thick black smoke fills his bedroom fast, leaving him under 60 seconds to make moves.", "start": 7.8, "end": 11.16}, {"text": "One. Get low and go right away because dangerous smoke always rises to the ceiling.", "start": 11.733, "end": 15.44}, {"text": "The cleanest air is near the floor, so Leo crouches low to breathe safely inside.", "start": 15.9, "end": 18.86}, {"text": "Two. Feel the door with the back of your hand before opening it to leave.", "start": 19.523, "end": 22.04}, {"text": "If the door is hot, do not open it, and use another way out fast.", "start": 22.52, "end": 25.32}, {"text": "Leo touches the wooden door with the back of his hand and feels cool surface.", "start": 26.08, "end": 28.84}, {"text": "Three. Close doors behind you as you move forward to slow down the fire spread.", "start": 29.736, "end": 32.64}, {"text": "Leo shuts the heavy bedroom door behind himself to block incoming heat and smoke.", "start": 33.14, "end": 36.32}, {"text": "He runs away out of the house into the cool night air to safety.", "start": 36.84, "end": 39.44}, {"text": "Official advice says get out, stay out, and call for help from outside always.", "start": 40.0, "end": 43.36}, {"text": "You must never go back inside a burning building for any reason at all.", "start": 43.94, "end": 46.54}, {"text": "Raging fire suddenly explodes through the roof, blasting heat across the entire front yard.", "start": 47.14, "end": 50.66}, {"text": "It was the perfect escape plan, but there was just one major problem remaining.", "start": 51.18, "end": 54.46}, {"text": "Leo needs to call for help, but his phone is still sitting inside.", "start": 55.24, "end": 58.2}], "words": [["I